{number: 118}
{title: I’d Rather Have Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I'd [C] rather have Jesus than [F] silver or [C] gold;
I'd rather be His than have [G7] riches untold;
I'd [C] rather have Jesus than [F] houses or [C] lands,
I'd rather be led by His [G7] nail-pierced [C] hands.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Than to [G7] be the king of a [C] vast domain
And be [G7] held in sin's dread [C] sway;
I'd [C] rather have Jesus than [F] anything
This [C] world af-[G7] fords to-[C] day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I'd [C] rather have Jesus than [F] men's ap-[C] plause;
I'd rather be faithful to [G7] His dear cause;
I'd [C] rather have Jesus than [F] worldwide [C] fame,
I'd rather be true to His [G7] holy [C] name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He's [C] fairer than lilies of [F] rarest [C] bloom;
He's sweeter than honey from [G7] out the comb;
He's [C] all that my hungering [F] spirit [C] needs,
I'd rather have Jesus and [G7] let Him [C] lead.
{end_of_verse}
